(function(E){ const x = E["exam-06"] = E["exam-06"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x06-r3"] = {"id":"x06-r3","patterns":["RA-tech","GT3-life","PARA-research"],"title":{"en":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","tr":"Reading 3: Passage 3 / Section 3","fa":"Reading ۳: متن ۳ (Passage 3) / بخش ۳ (Section 3)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide whether statements match the writer’s views, complete a summary from a box of words, and answer multiple-choice questions on the writer’s argument.","tr":"Bu derste ifadelerin yazarın görüşlerine uyup uymadığına karar vermeyi, bir özeti kelime kutusundan tamamlamayı ve yazarın argümanıyla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری تصمیم بگیری جمله‌ها با نظر نویسنده جورند یا نه، یک خلاصه را از روی کادر کلمه‌ها کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی استدلال نویسنده جواب بدهی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer multiple-choice questions on a long article, match opinions to the five people who give them, and complete a summary with one word from the text.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir yazı üzerine çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı, görüşleri onları dile getiren beş kişiyle eşleştirmeyi ve bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی یک مقاله‌ی بلند جواب بدهی، نظرها را به پنج نفری که آن‌ها را می‌گویند وصل کنی و یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 3: an argument about technology","tr":"Reading Passage 3: teknoloji üzerine bir tartışma","fa":"Reading Passage 3: استدلالی درباره‌ی فناوری"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide whether statements match the writer’s views, complete a summary from a box of words, and answer multiple-choice questions on the writer’s argument.","tr":"Bu derste ifadelerin yazarın görüşlerine uyup uymadığına karar vermeyi, bir özeti kelime kutusundan tamamlamayı ve yazarın argümanıyla ilgili çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری تصمیم بگیری جمله‌ها با نظر نویسنده جورند یا نه، یک خلاصه را از روی کادر کلمه‌ها کامل کنی و به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی استدلال نویسنده جواب بدهی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words in the box","tr":"Kutudaki kelime","fa":"کلمه‌های کادر"},"value":"A-H"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: video referees","tr":"Bu sınav: video hakemler","fa":"این آزمون: داورهای ویدیویی"},"intro":{"en":"Technology and its effects on society are a regular Passage 3 subject. The writer argues a position, so the YES/NO/NOT GIVEN questions test whether you can separate the writer’s opinion from facts and from other people’s views.","tr":"Teknoloji ve topluma etkileri düzenli bir Passage 3 konusudur. Yazar bir tutumu savunur; bu yüzden YES/NO/NOT GIVEN soruları yazarın görüşünü olgulardan ve başkalarının görüşlerinden ayırıp ayıramadığını ölçer.","fa":"فناوری و اثرش بر جامعه موضوع همیشگی Passage 3 است. نویسنده از یک موضع دفاع می‌کند، پس سؤال‌های YES/NO/NOT GIVEN می‌سنجند که می‌توانی نظر نویسنده را از واقعیت‌ها و نظر دیگران جدا کنی یا نه."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r3-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"An argument about technology in sport","tr":"Sporda teknoloji üzerine bir tartışma yazısı","fa":"استدلالی درباره‌ی فناوری در ورزش"},"asks":{"en":"A writer judges a new technology: what it was meant to do, what it has achieved, what it has made worse, how other sports do it better, and what should change. Every paragraph mixes facts with the writer’s own opinion.","tr":"Bir yazar yeni bir teknolojiyi değerlendiriyor: ne yapması amaçlanmıştı, neyi başardı, neyi daha kötü yaptı, diğer sporlar bunu nasıl daha iyi yapıyor ve ne değişmeli. Her paragraf olguları yazarın kendi görüşüyle karıştırıyor.","fa":"نویسنده‌ای یک فناوری تازه را می‌سنجد: قرار بود چه کند، چه چیزی به دست آورده، چه چیزی را بدتر کرده، ورزش‌های دیگر چطور بهتر عمل می‌کنند و چه چیزی باید عوض شود. هر پاراگراف واقعیت‌ها را با نظر خود نویسنده قاطی می‌کند."},"fields":["The scene","The case for","What it has not done","The cost","Other sports","A technical problem","Referees","Conclusion"],"words":[{"a":"I never believed","b":"I did not expect / it was naive to think","tr":"hiç inanmadım","fa":"هیچ‌وقت باور نداشتم"},{"a":"a matter of judgement","b":"depends on interpretation / not a fact","tr":"bir yorum meselesi","fa":"موضوعی سلیقه‌ای و تفسیری"},{"a":"the wrong way round","b":"the opposite of what it should be","tr":"tam tersi","fa":"برعکسِ چیزی که باید باشد"},{"a":"worst-informed","b":"know the least about what is happening","tr":"en az bilgilendirilmiş","fa":"کم‌اطلاع‌ترین"},{"a":"cautiously","b":"slowly and carefully","tr":"temkinli şekilde","fa":"با احتیاط"},{"a":"an illusion","b":"something that seems real but is not","tr":"bir yanılsama","fa":"یک توهم"},{"a":"benefit of the doubt","b":"decide in someone’s favour when unsure","tr":"şüpheden yararlandırmak","fa":"به نفع کسی تصمیم گرفتن وقتی مطمئن نیستی"},{"a":"divided","b":"some say one thing, others another","tr":"bölünmüş","fa":"دودسته"},{"a":"reluctant","b":"unwilling / prefer not to","tr":"isteksiz","fa":"بی‌میل"},{"a":"no firm evidence","b":"not yet proven","tr":"kesin kanıt yok","fa":"شاهد قطعی نیست"},{"a":"abandoned","b":"given up completely","tr":"bırakılmış, vazgeçilmiş","fa":"کنار گذاشته شده"},{"a":"in my view","b":"I believe / my argument is","tr":"bence","fa":"به نظر من"}],"traps":[{"en":"NOT GIVEN in a YES/NO task: the writer says something \"worries me\" but \"there is no firm evidence\". A statement that it has already happened is NOT GIVEN, not YES.","tr":"YES/NO görevinde NOT GIVEN: yazar bir şeyin onu \"endişelendirdiğini\" ama \"kesin kanıt olmadığını\" söylüyor. Bunun zaten olduğunu söyleyen bir ifade YES değil NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"NOT GIVEN در تمرین YES/NO: نویسنده می‌گوید چیزی «نگرانش می‌کند» اما «شاهد قطعی‌ای نیست». جمله‌ای که بگوید این اتفاق افتاده NOT GIVEN است، نه YES."},{"en":"Summary with a box: two box words can both fit the grammar (attacker, defender). Only one matches the writer’s suggestion.","tr":"Kutulu özet: kutudaki iki kelime de dil bilgisine uyabilir (attacker, defender). Yalnızca biri yazarın önerisine uyar.","fa":"خلاصه با کادر: ممکن است دو کلمه‌ی کادر هر دو از نظر دستوری جا شوند (attacker، defender). فقط یکی با پیشنهاد نویسنده جور است."},{"en":"Multiple choice about the writer’s overall view: one option takes a single criticism as if it were the conclusion.","tr":"Yazarın genel görüşüyle ilgili çoktan seçmeli soru: bir seçenek tek bir eleştiriyi sonuçmuş gibi sunar.","fa":"سؤال چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی نظر کلی نویسنده: یک گزینه یک انتقاد تنها را طوری می‌آورد که انگار نتیجه‌گیری است."}],"example":{"text":"\"Some coaches say the new ball is harder to control. I have never played with it, so I cannot judge.\"","item":"Statement: The new ball is harder to control. YES, NO or NOT GIVEN (views of the writer)?","answer":"NOT GIVEN","why":{"en":"The coaches say it; the writer \"cannot judge\", so the writer’s view is impossible to know.","tr":"Bunu antrenörler söylüyor; yazar \"değerlendiremem\" diyor, yani yazarın görüşünü bilmek imkânsız.","fa":"این را مربی‌ها می‌گویند؛ نویسنده می‌گوید «نمی‌توانم قضاوت کنم»، پس دانستن نظر نویسنده ممکن نیست."}}},{"id":"RA-tech-debate","ctx":["RA-tech"],"title":{"en":"Debates about new technology","tr":"Yeni teknoloji üzerine tartışmalar","fa":"بحث درباره‌ی فناوری‌های تازه"},"asks":{"en":"A discussion of a new technology: robot referees, artificial intelligence, space travel, cashless payment. The writer weighs benefits against risks; YES/NO/NOT GIVEN and multiple choice test the writer’s conclusion.","tr":"Yeni bir teknolojinin tartışıldığı bir metin: robot hakemler, yapay zekâ, uzay yolculuğu, nakitsiz ödeme. Yazar yararları risklerle tartar; YES/NO/NOT GIVEN ve çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın vardığı sonucu sınar.","fa":"بحثی درباره‌ی یک فناوری تازه: داور رباتیک، هوش مصنوعی، سفر فضایی، پرداخت بدون پول نقد. نویسنده فایده‌ها را با خطرها می‌سنجد؛ YES/NO/NOT GIVEN و چندگزینه‌ای نتیجه‌گیری نویسنده را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["The writer believes the technology will soon replace people. (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","According to the writer, the main risk is...","The writer mentions the 2018 match to show...","Summary: supporters claim the system is more ___ than people."],"words":[{"a":"replace","b":"take over from / do the job of","tr":"yerini almak","fa":"جایگزین شدن"},{"a":"accurate","b":"precise / makes fewer mistakes","tr":"isabetli","fa":"دقیق"},{"a":"risk","b":"danger / threat","tr":"risk","fa":"خطر"},{"a":"inevitable","b":"will certainly happen","tr":"kaçınılmaz","fa":"اجتناب‌ناپذیر"},{"a":"premature","b":"too early","tr":"erken","fa":"زودهنگام"},{"a":"transparency","b":"being open about how it works","tr":"şeffaflık","fa":"شفافیت"},{"a":"trust","b":"confidence in it","tr":"güven","fa":"اعتماد"},{"a":"flawed","b":"has faults / imperfect","tr":"kusurlu","fa":"معیوب"},{"a":"outweigh","b":"be greater than","tr":"ağır basmak","fa":"بیشتر بودن از"},{"a":"human judgement","b":"people deciding","tr":"insan muhakemesi","fa":"قضاوت انسانی"},{"a":"in theory","b":"on paper / in principle","tr":"teoride","fa":"در تئوری"},{"a":"in practice","b":"when it is actually used","tr":"pratikte","fa":"در عمل"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"In theory... in practice\": the writer usually believes what comes after \"in practice\".","tr":"\"Teoride... pratikte\": yazar genelde \"pratikte\"den sonra geleni savunur.","fa":"«در تئوری... در عمل»: نویسنده معمولاً به چیزی باور دارد که بعد از «در عمل» می‌آید."},{"en":"A prediction made by \"supporters\" is not the writer’s own prediction.","tr":"\"Destekçilerin\" yaptığı tahmin yazarın kendi tahmini değildir.","fa":"پیش‌بینیِ «طرفداران» پیش‌بینی خود نویسنده نیست."}],"example":{"text":"In theory, an automated referee never misses a foul. In practice, the systems tested so far have struggled in crowded penalty areas, and players have found it hard to accept decisions they cannot question.","item":"Statement: The writer believes automated referees already work well in every situation.  (YES / NO / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"NO","why":{"en":"\"In practice... have struggled\" contradicts \"work well in every situation\".","tr":"\"Pratikte... zorlandılar\", \"her durumda iyi çalışıyor\" ile çelişir.","fa":"«در عمل... به مشکل خوردند» با «در هر موقعیتی خوب کار می‌کنند» در تضاد است."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-tech"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Views, a box, then four options","tr":"Görüşler, bir kutu, sonra dört seçenek","fa":"نظرها، یک کادر، بعد چهار گزینه"},"body":{"en":"Questions 27-32: YES, NO or NOT GIVEN about the writer’s views. Questions 33-37: complete a summary with words from a box, A-H; three words are not used. Questions 38-40: choose A, B, C or D. All three tasks follow the passage.","tr":"Soru 27-32: yazarın görüşleri hakkında YES, NO ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 33-37: A-H kutusundaki kelimelerle bir özeti tamamla; üç kelime kullanılmaz. Soru 38-40: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç. Üç görev de metni izler.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۷ تا ۳۲: YES، NO یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی نظرهای نویسنده. سؤال‌های ۳۳ تا ۳۷: یک خلاصه را با کلمه‌های کادر A تا H کامل کن؛ سه کلمه استفاده نمی‌شوند. سؤال‌های ۳۸ تا ۴۰: A، B، C یا D را انتخاب کن. هر سه تمرین ترتیب متن را دنبال می‌کنند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Listen for the writer’s voice","tr":"Yazarın sesine kulak ver","fa":"صدای نویسنده را پیدا کن"},"steps":[{"en":"Mark the writer’s opinion words in the passage: in my view, I believe, I never believed, worries me.","tr":"Metinde yazarın görüş kelimelerini işaretle: in my view, I believe, I never believed, worries me.","fa":"کلمه‌های نظرِ نویسنده را در متن علامت بزن: in my view، I believe، I never believed، worries me."},{"en":"For each statement, find the place and ask: does the writer agree, disagree, or not say?","tr":"Her ifade için yeri bul ve sor: yazar katılıyor mu, karşı mı, yoksa bir şey söylemiyor mu?","fa":"برای هر جمله جایش را پیدا کن و بپرس: نویسنده موافق است، مخالف است یا چیزی نمی‌گوید؟"},{"en":"For the box, decide the word class of each gap before you look at the box words.","tr":"Kutu için, kutudaki kelimelere bakmadan önce her boşluğun kelime türüne karar ver.","fa":"برای کادر، قبل از نگاه کردن به کلمه‌ها، نوع کلمه‌ی هر جای خالی را مشخص کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"A worry is not a fact","tr":"Bir endişe bir olgu değildir","fa":"نگرانی یعنی واقعیت نیست"},"body":{"en":"Writers often say what they fear might happen and add that it is not proven. A statement that the thing has already happened is then NOT GIVEN. Similarly, what other people promised or claimed is not the writer’s view.","tr":"Yazarlar çoğu zaman olmasından korktukları şeyi söyler ve bunun kanıtlanmadığını ekler. Bunun zaten olduğunu söyleyen bir ifade o zaman NOT GIVEN’dır. Benzer şekilde, başkalarının vaat ettiği ya da iddia ettiği şey yazarın görüşü değildir.","fa":"نویسنده‌ها اغلب می‌گویند از چه چیزی می‌ترسند و اضافه می‌کنند که ثابت نشده. جمله‌ای که بگوید آن اتفاق افتاده در این حالت NOT GIVEN است. به همین ترتیب، چیزی که دیگران قول داده یا ادعا کرده‌اند نظر نویسنده نیست."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"A summary-box gap, step by step","tr":"Kutulu bir özet boşluğu, adım adım","fa":"یک جای خالیِ خلاصه با کادر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Complete the summary using the list of words, A-D.","text":"\"In hockey, umpires can ask for a replay, but each team may only challenge one decision per half.\"","item":"Summary: Each team is allowed one ___ per half.  A replay  B challenge  C umpire  D decision","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The gap follows \"one\", so it needs a singular noun: all four could fit the grammar.","tr":"Boşluk \"one\"dan sonra geliyor, yani tekil bir isim gerekiyor: dördü de dil bilgisine uyabilir.","fa":"جای خالی بعد از «one» است، پس اسم مفرد می‌خواهد: هر چهار کلمه از نظر دستوری جا می‌شوند."},{"en":"\"May only challenge one decision\" = is allowed one challenge.","tr":"\"Yalnızca bir karara itiraz edebilir\" = bir itiraz hakkı var.","fa":"«فقط می‌تواند به یک تصمیم اعتراض کند» یعنی یک اعتراض مجاز است."},{"en":"Decision and replay appear in the sentence but do not give the right meaning: B.","tr":"Decision ve replay cümlede geçiyor ama doğru anlamı vermiyor: B.","fa":"decision و replay در جمله هستند اما معنی درست را نمی‌دهند: B."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"Supporters of the scheme promised it would end traffic jams. I always doubted this.\" Statement: \"The writer expected the scheme to end traffic jams.\" YES, NO or NOT GIVEN?","options":["YES","NO","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The supporters promised it; the writer \"always doubted this\", which contradicts the statement.","tr":"Bunu destekçiler vaat etti; yazar \"buna hep şüpheyle baktı\", bu da ifadeyle çelişiyor.","fa":"طرفدارها این قول را دادند؛ نویسنده «همیشه به آن شک داشت» که با جمله تناقض دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"Find the writer’s own voice, treat worries and promises as different from facts, and decide the word class before using the box.","tr":"Yazarın kendi sesini bul, endişeleri ve vaatleri olgulardan ayrı tut ve kutuyu kullanmadan önce kelime türüne karar ver.","fa":"صدای خود نویسنده را پیدا کن، نگرانی‌ها و قول‌ها را از واقعیت جدا بدان و قبل از استفاده از کادر نوع کلمه را مشخص کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r3-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 3","title":{"en":"Waiting for the screen","tr":"Ekranı beklerken","fa":"در انتظار صفحه‌ی نمایش"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-tech"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading Passage 3 below.","passage":"Waiting for the screen\n\nThe ball hits the net, the players race towards the corner flag, and thousands of supporters leap from their seats. Then, gradually, everyone turns to look at the referee, who is standing in the centre circle with one finger pressed to his ear. The celebration is on hold. Since video assistant referees were introduced into professional football, this scene has become familiar in stadiums around the world. My argument in this article is that the system has got the most important thing right, and a surprising number of smaller things wrong.\n\nThe case for video is easy to make. Football is fast, and a single referee, however fit and experienced, cannot see everything. For years, television showed millions of viewers slow-motion replays that made a referee's mistake obvious within seconds, while the referee alone was left to defend it. With a single goal able to decide a championship, or to send a club down to a lower division, the cost of such mistakes had become enormous, both for the clubs involved and for the reputation of referees themselves. On the evidence available, video has done what it was meant to do: the most important decisions, such as whether a goal should stand, are now right far more often than before.\n\nWhat it has not done is end the arguments, and those who promised that it would were naive. I never believed that technology would remove controversy from football, because so many decisions are matters of judgement rather than fact. Whether a defender's arm was in an \"unnatural position\", or whether a push was strong enough to justify a penalty, depends on interpretation, and two officials watching the same replay can still disagree. Slow motion can even make the problem worse, because ordinary contact between players looks far more violent when it is slowed down. The argument has simply moved from the pitch to the screen.\n\nThe greatest cost, in my view, is to the experience of the people in the stadium. A video check can take several minutes, during which the crowd usually has no idea what is being examined or why. Viewers at home, meanwhile, are shown replay after replay from every angle. This is exactly the wrong way round. The supporters who have paid to be there, and who create the atmosphere that makes the game worth watching, are the worst-informed people in the country. Many simply stop celebrating goals until the referee has confirmed them, which takes away one of the great pleasures of being a fan.\n\nOther sports have found better solutions. In rugby union, the conversation between the referee and the video official can be heard by the crowd, and the replays they are studying are shown on large screens inside the ground. Spectators may not agree with the decision, but they understand how it was reached. Football's authorities have moved in this direction only slowly and cautiously, and I believe they should go much further.\n\nOffside decisions raise a different problem. Officials now draw lines on frozen images to decide whether an attacker was ahead of the last defender, sometimes by a margin of a few centimetres. The difficulty is that the result can depend on which of the frames is chosen as the moment the ball was played, since a camera captures only a limited number of images each second. Precision of this kind is partly an illusion. A sensible reform would accept a small margin of error and, when a decision is genuinely too close to call, give the benefit of the doubt to the attacker, as the original spirit of the rule intended.\n\nReferees themselves are divided about the system. Some say that it has taken an unbearable pressure off their shoulders, since they know that a serious error will be corrected. Others feel that their authority on the pitch has been weakened, because players and spectators now look past them to the screen. There is a further risk that worries me more. Young referees who have never worked without video may become reluctant to make difficult decisions themselves, preferring to wait for a second opinion. There is not yet any firm evidence that this is happening, but it would be a serious loss if it did.\n\nNone of this means that video should be abandoned. The game is fairer than it was, and few people would want to return to the days when an obvious handball could win a cup final. But the system needs to change: checks should have a strict time limit, decisions should be explained to the crowd as they are made, and officials should step in only when an error is clear. Accuracy matters, but so does the experience of watching the game.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 27-32. Do the following statements agree with the views of the writer in Reading Passage 3? In boxes 27-32 on your answer sheet, write YES if the statement agrees with the views of the writer, NO if the statement contradicts the views of the writer, NOT GIVEN if it is impossible to say what the writer thinks about this.","qtype":"ynng","questions":[{"n":27,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Video has made the most important refereeing decisions more accurate.","correct":"YES","evidence":"are now right far more often than before","why":{"en":"\"Video has done what it was meant to do: the most important decisions... are now right far more often than before.\"","tr":"\"Video yapması gerekeni yaptı: en önemli kararlar... artık eskisinden çok daha sık doğru.\"","fa":"«ویدیو کاری را که قرار بود بکند کرده: مهم‌ترین تصمیم‌ها... حالا خیلی بیشتر از قبل درست‌اند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":28,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"The writer expected video to put an end to arguments about refereeing.","correct":"NO","evidence":"I never believed that technology would remove controversy from football","why":{"en":"Others promised it; the writer \"never believed that technology would remove controversy\".","tr":"Bunu başkaları vaat etti; yazar \"teknolojinin tartışmayı ortadan kaldıracağına hiç inanmadı\".","fa":"دیگران این قول را دادند؛ نویسنده «هیچ‌وقت باور نداشت فناوری جنجال را از بین ببرد»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":29,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Slow-motion replays can make contact between players look more serious than it was.","correct":"YES","evidence":"ordinary contact between players looks far more violent when it is slowed down","why":{"en":"\"Ordinary contact between players looks far more violent when it is slowed down.\"","tr":"\"Oyuncular arasındaki sıradan temas yavaşlatıldığında çok daha sert görünüyor.\"","fa":"«برخورد معمولی بین بازیکن‌ها وقتی آهسته پخش شود خیلی خشن‌تر به نظر می‌رسد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Spectators in the stadium are better informed than viewers at home.","correct":"NO","evidence":"are the worst-informed people in the country","why":{"en":"The writer calls it \"exactly the wrong way round\": spectators \"are the worst-informed people in the country\".","tr":"Yazar buna \"tam tersi\" diyor: seyirciler \"ülkedeki en az bilgilendirilmiş insanlar\".","fa":"نویسنده می‌گوید «دقیقاً برعکس است»: تماشاگرهای ورزشگاه «کم‌اطلاع‌ترین آدم‌های کشورند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":31,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Rugby players prefer their video system to the one used in football.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Spectators may not agree with the decision, but they understand how it was reached","why":{"en":"The writer describes what rugby spectators can see and hear; players’ opinions are not mentioned.","tr":"Yazar rugby seyircilerinin ne görüp duyabildiğini anlatıyor; oyuncuların görüşlerinden söz edilmiyor.","fa":"نویسنده می‌گوید تماشاگرهای راگبی چه می‌بینند و می‌شنوند؛ از نظر بازیکن‌ها حرفی نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":32,"kind":"ynng","prompt":"Video has made young referees less willing to make difficult decisions.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"There is not yet any firm evidence that this is happening","why":{"en":"This is a risk that \"worries\" the writer, but \"there is not yet any firm evidence\" that it is happening.","tr":"Bu, yazarı \"endişelendiren\" bir risk ama bunun olduğuna dair \"henüz kesin bir kanıt yok\".","fa":"این خطری است که نویسنده را «نگران می‌کند»، اما «هنوز هیچ شاهد قطعی‌ای نیست» که اتفاق بیفتد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-whosevoice"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 33-37. Complete the summary using the list of words, A-H, below. Write the correct letter, A-H, in boxes 33-37 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary-box","summaryTitle":"Other sports and offside decisions","bank":["A heard","B replays","C centimetres","D faster","E attacker","F defender","G slower","H frames"],"questions":[{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"In rugby union, the conversation between the referee and the video official can be ___ by the crowd,","correct":0,"evidence":"can be heard by the crowd","why":{"en":"\"Can be heard by the crowd\". The past participle heard fits \"can be ___\".","tr":"\"Seyirci tarafından duyulabilir\". Geçmiş ortaç heard, \"can be ___\" yapısına uyuyor.","fa":"«تماشاگرها می‌توانند بشنوند». اسم مفعولِ heard با «can be ___» جور است."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"who can also watch the ___ on large screens.","correct":1,"evidence":"the replays they are studying are shown on large screens","why":{"en":"\"The replays they are studying are shown on large screens inside the ground.\"","tr":"\"İncelenen tekrarlar stadyumdaki büyük ekranlarda gösteriliyor.\"","fa":"«تکرارهایی که بررسی می‌کنند روی صفحه‌های بزرگ داخل ورزشگاه نشان داده می‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"In football, an offside decision may come down to a few ___,","correct":2,"evidence":"sometimes by a margin of a few centimetres","why":{"en":"\"Sometimes by a margin of a few centimetres.\"","tr":"\"Bazen birkaç santimetrelik bir farkla.\"","fa":"«گاهی با فاصله‌ای چندسانتی‌متری»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":36,"kind":"match","prompt":"and the result can depend on which of the camera ___ is chosen.","correct":7,"evidence":"which of the frames is chosen","why":{"en":"\"The result can depend on which of the frames is chosen.\" Replays (B) is already used and does not fit \"which of the camera ___ is chosen\".","tr":"\"Sonuç hangi karenin seçildiğine bağlı olabilir.\" Replays (B) zaten kullanıldı ve buraya uymuyor.","fa":"«نتیجه ممکن است به این بستگی داشته باشد که کدام فریم انتخاب شود». replays (B) قبلاً استفاده شده و این‌جا جور نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":37,"kind":"match","prompt":"The writer suggests that, when a decision is too close to call, it should favour the ___.","correct":4,"evidence":"give the benefit of the doubt to the attacker","why":{"en":"\"Give the benefit of the doubt to the attacker\" = favour the attacker. Defender (F) fits the grammar but not the meaning.","tr":"\"Şüpheden hücum oyuncusunu yararlandırmak\" = hücum oyuncusunu kayırmak. Defender (F) dil bilgisine uyar ama anlama uymaz.","fa":"«به نفع مهاجم تصمیم گرفتن در موارد شک» یعنی طرفداری از مهاجم. defender (F) از نظر دستوری جا می‌شود اما معنی‌اش نه."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 38-40. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 38-40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":38,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about referees’ views of video?","options":["A All referees welcome it.","B Referees do not agree about it.","C Most referees would like it removed.","D Referees were never asked for their opinion."],"correct":1,"evidence":"Referees themselves are divided about the system","why":{"en":"\"Referees themselves are divided\": some feel relieved, others feel their authority has been weakened.","tr":"\"Hakemlerin kendisi de bölünmüş durumda\": bazıları rahatlamış, bazıları otoritelerinin zayıfladığını düşünüyor.","fa":"«خود داورها دودسته‌اند»: بعضی‌ها احساس آسودگی می‌کنند و بعضی فکر می‌کنند اقتدارشان کم شده."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":39,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What worries the writer most about the future of refereeing?","options":["A Fans may stop going to matches.","B The technology may become too expensive.","C Young referees may rely too much on video.","D The offside rule may be changed."],"correct":2,"evidence":"may become reluctant to make difficult decisions themselves","why":{"en":"\"There is a further risk that worries me more\": young referees \"may become reluctant to make difficult decisions themselves\".","tr":"\"Beni daha çok endişelendiren bir risk daha var\": genç hakemler \"zor kararları kendileri vermekte isteksiz hâle gelebilir\".","fa":"«خطر دیگری هست که بیشتر نگرانم می‌کند»: داورهای جوان «ممکن است از گرفتن تصمیم‌های سخت به‌تنهایی پرهیز کنند»."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":40,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What is the writer’s overall opinion of video refereeing?","options":["A It should be abandoned.","B It has improved the experience of watching football.","C It should be introduced in every sport.","D It is worth keeping but needs to change."],"correct":3,"evidence":"None of this means that video should be abandoned","why":{"en":"\"None of this means that video should be abandoned... But the system needs to change.\" B contradicts the writer’s main criticism.","tr":"\"Bunların hiçbiri videonun bırakılması gerektiği anlamına gelmiyor... Ama sistemin değişmesi gerekiyor.\" B yazarın ana eleştirisiyle çelişiyor.","fa":"«هیچ‌کدام از این‌ها یعنی ویدیو باید کنار گذاشته شود نیست... اما سیستم باید عوض شود». B با انتقاد اصلی نویسنده تناقض دارد."},"trap":["TR-samewords","TR-whosevoice"]}]}],"id":"c-x06-r3-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Those who promised it would end every argument were naive.\" Naive means...","options":["too ready to believe something simple","very experienced","dishonest"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Naive = showing a lack of experience or judgement.","tr":"Naive = deneyim ya da muhakeme eksikliği gösteren, saf.","fa":"naive یعنی ساده‌لوح، کم‌تجربه در قضاوت."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"A summary says \"decide in favour of the attacker\". Which words in a passage mean the same?","options":["blame the attacker","ignore the attacker","give the benefit of the doubt to the attacker"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Giving someone the benefit of the doubt = deciding in their favour when you are not sure.","tr":"Birini şüpheden yararlandırmak = emin olmadığında onun lehine karar vermek.","fa":"دادن «benefit of the doubt» یعنی وقتی مطمئن نیستی به نفع او تصمیم بگیری."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Summary with a box of eight words and five gaps. What do you do first for each gap?","options":["choose the word you see most often in the passage","decide what kind of word fits the grammar","use the words in alphabetical order"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The grammar narrows the choice; then the meaning decides.","tr":"Dil bilgisi seçimi daraltır; sonra anlam karar verir.","fa":"دستور زبان انتخاب را محدود می‌کند؛ بعد معنی تصمیم می‌گیرد."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"One risk worries me: that fans will stop travelling to away games. So far, though, attendance is stable.\" Statement: \"Fans have stopped travelling to away games.\" (views of the writer)","options":["NOT GIVEN","YES","NO"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"This is only a worry; the text says nothing about away fans actually stopping, so the writer’s view on it cannot be known.","tr":"Bu yalnızca bir endişe; metin deplasman taraftarlarının gerçekten gitmeyi bıraktığına dair bir şey söylemiyor.","fa":"این فقط یک نگرانی است؛ متن نمی‌گوید هوادارها واقعاً دیگر به بازی‌های خارج از خانه نمی‌روند."}}],"id":"c-x06-r3-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 3: an article with five voices","tr":"GT Reading Section 3: beş sesli bir yazı","fa":"GT Reading Section 3: مقاله‌ای با پنج صدا"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to answer multiple-choice questions on a long article, match opinions to the five people who give them, and complete a summary with one word from the text.","tr":"Bu derste uzun bir yazı üzerine çoktan seçmeli soruları cevaplamayı, görüşleri onları dile getiren beş kişiyle eşleştirmeyi ve bir özeti metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری به سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای درباره‌ی یک مقاله‌ی بلند جواب بدهی، نظرها را به پنج نفری که آن‌ها را می‌گویند وصل کنی و یک خلاصه را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"People","tr":"Kişi","fa":"آدم‌ها"},"value":"A-E"},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~760"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: a school without homework","tr":"Bu sınav: ödevsiz bir okul","fa":"این آزمون: مدرسه‌ای بدون تکلیف خانه"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 3 is one long article for a general reader. Society, work and daily life are among the most common subjects. Articles about a change often quote several people with different views, which is what the matching task tests.","tr":"GT Section 3 genel okur için tek bir uzun yazıdır. Toplum, iş ve günlük yaşam en sık konulardandır. Bir değişiklik hakkındaki yazılar çoğu zaman farklı görüşte birkaç kişiden alıntı yapar; eşleştirme görevi bunu ölçer.","fa":"GT Section 3 یک مقاله‌ی بلند برای خواننده‌ی عمومی است. جامعه، کار و زندگی روزمره از رایج‌ترین موضوع‌ها هستند. مقاله‌هایی درباره‌ی یک تغییر اغلب از چند نفر با نظرهای متفاوت نقل‌قول می‌کنند و تمرین جورکردن همین را می‌سنجد."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x06-r3gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT3-life","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A school that tried something new","tr":"Yeni bir şey deneyen bir okul","fa":"مدرسه‌ای که چیز تازه‌ای را امتحان کرد"},"asks":{"en":"A magazine article about a change at a school, with the views of five people: the head teacher, a parent, a pupil, a researcher and a critic. You match each opinion to the person who holds it.","tr":"Bir okuldaki bir değişiklik hakkında, beş kişinin görüşlerini içeren bir dergi yazısı: müdür, bir veli, bir öğrenci, bir araştırmacı ve bir eleştirmen. Her görüşü onu savunan kişiyle eşleştirirsin.","fa":"مقاله‌ای در مجله درباره‌ی تغییری در یک مدرسه، با نظر پنج نفر: مدیر، یک والد، یک دانش‌آموز، یک پژوهشگر و یک منتقد. هر نظر را به کسی که آن را دارد وصل می‌کنی."},"fields":["The change","Why it happened","How it was introduced","Parents and pupils","The research","A critic","Results"],"words":[{"a":"the final straw","b":"the last reason that made them act","tr":"bardağı taşıran son damla","fa":"تیر آخر، دلیل نهایی"},{"a":"unconvinced","b":"not sure it works / doubtful","tr":"ikna olmamış","fa":"قانع‌نشده"},{"a":"fall behind","b":"learn less than others / not keep up","tr":"geride kalmak","fa":"عقب افتادن"},{"a":"relaxed","b":"calmer / less stressed","tr":"rahat","fa":"آرام"},{"a":"achievement","b":"results / how well children do","tr":"başarı","fa":"پیشرفت تحصیلی"},{"a":"widen the gap","b":"make differences bigger","tr":"aradaki farkı açmak","fa":"شکاف را بیشتر کردن"},{"a":"persuaded","b":"convinced","tr":"ikna olmuş","fa":"متقاعد"},{"a":"organise their time","b":"plan when to do things","tr":"zamanını düzenlemek","fa":"وقتش را مدیریت کردن"},{"a":"a fair point","b":"a reasonable criticism","tr":"haklı bir nokta","fa":"نکته‌ای منصفانه"},{"a":"optional","b":"you can choose / not checked or marked","tr":"isteğe bağlı","fa":"اختیاری"},{"a":"stayed much the same","b":"did not change very much","tr":"aşağı yukarı aynı kaldı","fa":"تقریباً همان ماند"}],"traps":[{"en":"Whose opinion? A person may report what others think: \"Some parents worried...\" is not that person’s own view.","tr":"Kimin görüşü? Biri başkalarının düşündüğünü aktarabilir: \"Bazı veliler endişelendi...\" o kişinin kendi görüşü değildir.","fa":"نظرِ کیست؟ ممکن است کسی نظر دیگران را نقل کند: «بعضی والدین نگران بودند...» نظر خود آن آدم نیست."},{"en":"One person can match two statements, and the same idea can be said in different words by different people. Read every quotation before choosing.","tr":"Bir kişi iki ifadeye uyabilir ve aynı fikir farklı kişiler tarafından farklı kelimelerle söylenebilir. Seçmeden önce her alıntıyı oku.","fa":"یک نفر ممکن است با دو جمله جور باشد و یک ایده را آدم‌های مختلف با کلمه‌های مختلف بگویند. قبل از انتخاب همه‌ی نقل‌قول‌ها را بخوان."}],"example":{"text":"\"‘It saves me time in the mornings,’ says Tom, a parent. The head teacher, Ms Reid, sees a different benefit: ‘Children arrive calmer.’\"","item":"Statement: Pupils are less stressed when they get to school. A Tom  B Ms Reid","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Tom talks about his own time; Ms Reid says \"children arrive calmer\".","tr":"Tom kendi zamanından söz ediyor; Bayan Reid \"çocuklar daha sakin geliyor\" diyor.","fa":"تام از وقت خودش حرف می‌زند؛ خانم رید می‌گوید «بچه‌ها آرام‌تر می‌رسند»."}}},{"id":"GT3-life","ctx":["GT3-life"],"title":{"en":"Society, work and daily life","tr":"Toplum, iş ve gündelik yaşam","fa":"جامعه، کار و زندگی روزمره"},"asks":{"en":"A text about modern life, work or society: a nursery without toys, emojis, a health programme, lessons in leadership, life in a cold town. Headings and multiple choice test the writer’s main points.","tr":"Modern yaşam, iş ya da toplum hakkında bir metin: oyuncaksız bir kreş, emojiler, bir sağlık programı, liderlik dersleri, soğuk bir kasabada yaşam. Başlıklar ve çoktan seçmeli sorular yazarın ana noktalarını sınar.","fa":"متنی درباره‌ی زندگی امروز، کار یا جامعه: مهدکودکی بدون اسباب‌بازی، ایموجی‌ها، یک برنامه‌ی سلامت، درس‌هایی درباره‌ی رهبری، زندگی در یک شهر سرد. عنوان‌ها و سؤال‌های چندگزینه‌ای نکته‌های اصلی نویسنده را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["An experiment that surprised parents","Mixed reactions from staff","The original purpose","Plans to expand the scheme","Which paragraph describes the results after a year?"],"words":[{"a":"scheme","b":"programme / project","tr":"program, uygulama","fa":"طرح"},{"a":"reaction","b":"response / what people thought","tr":"tepki","fa":"واکنش"},{"a":"mixed","b":"some liked it, others did not","tr":"karışık","fa":"دوگانه"},{"a":"surprising","b":"unexpected / few predicted it","tr":"şaşırtıcı","fa":"غافلگیرکننده"},{"a":"purpose","b":"aim / designed to","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"expand","b":"grow / extend to more places","tr":"genişletmek","fa":"گسترش دادن"},{"a":"residents","b":"locals / people who live there","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"wellbeing","b":"health and happiness","tr":"iyi oluş","fa":"سلامت و رضایت"},{"a":"communicate","b":"express / get a message across","tr":"iletişim kurmak","fa":"ارتباط برقرار کردن"},{"a":"encourage","b":"motivate / persuade","tr":"teşvik etmek","fa":"تشویق کردن"},{"a":"trend","b":"something becoming common","tr":"eğilim","fa":"روند"},{"a":"outcome","b":"result / what happened","tr":"sonuç","fa":"نتیجه"}],"traps":[{"en":"\"Mixed reactions\" needs both sides in the paragraph. One positive comment is not enough.","tr":"\"Karışık tepkiler\" için paragrafta iki taraf da olmalı. Tek bir olumlu yorum yetmez.","fa":"«واکنش‌های دوگانه» یعنی هر دو طرف در پاراگراف باشند. یک نظر مثبت کافی نیست."},{"en":"The purpose of a scheme and its result are often in different paragraphs.","tr":"Bir uygulamanın amacı ve sonucu çoğu zaman farklı paragraflardadır.","fa":"هدف یک طرح و نتیجه‌اش اغلب در پاراگراف‌های جدا هستند."}],"example":{"text":"E  Not everyone was convinced. Several parents worried that their children would be bored without toys, while a few teachers felt the experiment had started too quickly. Others, however, praised the calmer atmosphere.","item":"Choose the heading for paragraph E:  i  Mixed reactions   ii  Children become bored   iii  How the toys were chosen","answer":"i","why":{"en":"Worries from parents and teachers, then praise from others: both sides, so mixed reactions.","tr":"Ebeveyn ve öğretmenlerin endişeleri, ardından başkalarının övgüsü: iki taraf da var, yani karışık tepkiler.","fa":"نگرانی پدر و مادرها و معلم‌ها، بعد تعریف دیگران: هر دو طرف هست، پس واکنش‌های دوگانه."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT3-life"],"often":{"pattern":"GT3-life","n":14,"of":40,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 14 of the last 40 tests","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 40 sınavın 14’ünde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۴ آزمون از ۴۰ آزمونِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Three tasks on one article","tr":"Bir yazı üzerinde üç görev","fa":"سه تمرین روی یک مقاله"},"body":{"en":"Questions 28-30: choose A, B, C or D. Questions 31-35: match each statement to one of five people, A-E; a letter can be used more than once. Questions 36-40: complete a summary with ONE WORD ONLY from the text.","tr":"Soru 28-30: A, B, C ya da D’yi seç. Soru 31-35: her ifadeyi A-E arası beş kişiden biriyle eşleştir; bir harf birden fazla kullanılabilir. Soru 36-40: bir özeti metinden ONE WORD ONLY ile tamamla.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۲۸ تا ۳۰: A، B، C یا D را انتخاب کن. سؤال‌های ۳۱ تا ۳۵: هر جمله را به یکی از پنج نفر، A تا E، وصل کن؛ یک حرف می‌تواند بیش از یک بار بیاید. سؤال‌های ۳۶ تا ۴۰: یک خلاصه را با ONE WORD ONLY از متن کامل کن."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Find each person, then their words","tr":"Önce her kişiyi, sonra sözlerini bul","fa":"اول هر نفر را پیدا کن، بعد حرف‌هایش را"},"steps":[{"en":"Circle the five names in the text: each person usually has one paragraph.","tr":"Metindeki beş ismi daire içine al: her kişinin genelde bir paragrafı vardır.","fa":"دور پنج اسم در متن خط بکش: هر نفر معمولاً یک پاراگراف دارد."},{"en":"Read each statement and look for the person whose own words mean the same.","tr":"Her ifadeyi oku ve kendi sözleri aynı anlama gelen kişiyi ara.","fa":"هر جمله را بخوان و دنبال کسی بگرد که حرف خودش همان معنی را دارد."},{"en":"For the summary, find the paragraph it covers, then copy one word in the form the gap needs.","tr":"Özet için kapsadığı paragrafı bul, sonra boşluğun istediği biçimde tek kelimeyi kopyala.","fa":"برای خلاصه، پاراگرافی را که پوشش می‌دهد پیدا کن و بعد یک کلمه را به شکلی که جای خالی می‌خواهد کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Reported views","tr":"Aktarılan görüşler","fa":"نظرهای نقل‌شده"},"body":{"en":"People in an article often mention other people’s opinions before giving their own: \"Some parents worried...\" or \"Others said it would never work.\" Match a statement only to the person who actually holds that view.","tr":"Bir yazıdaki kişiler çoğu zaman kendi görüşlerini vermeden önce başkalarının görüşlerinden söz eder: \"Bazı veliler endişelendi...\" ya da \"Başkaları bunun asla işe yaramayacağını söyledi.\" Bir ifadeyi yalnızca o görüşe gerçekten sahip olan kişiyle eşleştir.","fa":"آدم‌های یک مقاله اغلب قبل از گفتن نظر خودشان از نظر دیگران حرف می‌زنند: «بعضی والدین نگران بودند...» یا «دیگران گفتند هیچ‌وقت جواب نمی‌دهد». جمله را فقط به کسی وصل کن که واقعاً همان نظر را دارد."}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"Matching a person, step by step","tr":"Bir kişiyi eşleştirmek, adım adım","fa":"وصل کردن یک نفر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Match the statement with the correct person.","text":"\"‘People told us the new timetable would confuse everyone,’ says Ana, the manager. ‘In fact, staff picked it up in a week.’\"","item":"Statement: Staff found the new timetable confusing. Does this match Ana?","answer":"No","walk":[{"en":"Find Ana’s words in the text.","tr":"Metinde Ana’nın sözlerini bul.","fa":"حرف‌های آنا را در متن پیدا کن."},{"en":"\"People told us... would confuse everyone\" is what other people said.","tr":"\"İnsanlar bize... herkesin kafasını karıştıracağını söyledi\" başkalarının söylediği şey.","fa":"«مردم به ما گفتند... همه را گیج می‌کند» حرف دیگران است."},{"en":"Her own view: \"staff picked it up in a week\". The statement does not match Ana.","tr":"Kendi görüşü: \"personel bir haftada öğrendi\". İfade Ana’ya uymuyor.","fa":"نظر خودش: «کارکنان یک‌هفته‌ای یاد گرفتند». جمله با آنا جور نیست."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"‘Some colleagues think the change was a mistake,’ says Leo. ‘I can see why, but I think it was right.’\" What is Leo’s own view?","options":["The change was a mistake.","He is not sure.","The change was right."],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"He reports his colleagues’ view, then gives his own: \"I think it was right.\"","tr":"Meslektaşlarının görüşünü aktarıyor, sonra kendininkini veriyor: \"Bence doğruydu.\"","fa":"نظر همکارهایش را نقل می‌کند و بعد نظر خودش را می‌دهد: «به نظرم درست بود»."}},"remember":{"en":"Circle the names, match each statement to the person’s own words, and copy one word for the summary.","tr":"İsimleri daire içine al, her ifadeyi kişinin kendi sözleriyle eşleştir ve özet için tek kelime kopyala.","fa":"دور اسم‌ها خط بکش، هر جمله را با حرف خود آن آدم جور کن و برای خلاصه یک کلمه کپی کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x06-r3-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 3","title":{"en":"The school that stopped setting homework","tr":"Ödev vermeyi bırakan okul","fa":"مدرسه‌ای که دیگر تکلیف نداد"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT3-life"],"texts":[{"title":"The school that stopped setting homework","kind":"article","body":"Two years ago, Brookfield Primary School in the north of the city made a decision that surprised many parents: it stopped setting homework for all its pupils, from the youngest five-year-olds to the eleven-year-olds in their final year. Instead, every child is asked to read for twenty minutes a day, for pleasure, choosing whatever they like.\n\nThe idea did not come from the teachers, at least not at first. \"Marking homework took up a lot of our time, but that was never the main reason,\" says the head teacher, Ruth Adeyemi. \"The final straw was a survey we sent to parents. When we asked what caused the most arguments at home, homework came top by a long way.\" Adeyemi was also unconvinced that the worksheets the school sent home were teaching children very much. \"A child who reads a book they love for twenty minutes learns more than a child who fills in a worksheet they hate,\" she says. \"I'm completely sure of that.\"\n\nThe change was introduced carefully. The school first held two evening meetings for parents, explained the research it had read, and agreed to try the new approach for one year before making a final decision. Teachers sent home a list of suggested books for each age group, and the school library began opening for half an hour after lessons so that children could borrow books on their way home. Families were also given ideas for optional projects, such as planting seeds, writing a short diary or interviewing a grandparent about their childhood. None of these is checked or marked. \"We wanted to give parents something to do if they asked for it,\" Adeyemi explains, \"without turning it into homework by another name.\" At the end of the trial year, a second survey found that more than three quarters of parents wanted to continue.\n\nNot every family welcomed the change. Some parents worried that their children would fall behind, and a few moved them to other schools. But many describe a very different atmosphere at home. Gareth Lyle, whose two sons are in Years 3 and 5, says the biggest difference is time. \"They used to come home and sit at the kitchen table for an hour, usually in tears. Now they go to football training, help me cook, or just play outside. They're much more relaxed children.\"\n\nThe pupils seem to agree. Eleven-year-old Sofia, who is in her last year at Brookfield, says she reads far more than she used to. \"Before, I only read the books we were given. Now I choose my own, and I've read all of one fantasy series twice.\" What she likes most, though, is that evenings are calmer. \"My mum and I used to argue about homework every night. We don't any more.\"\n\nResearch on homework is less clear than either side of the debate often suggests. Professor Ines Duarte, who studies primary education, points out that for children under eleven, homework appears to have very little effect on achievement. \"There may be some benefit in helping children develop study habits,\" she says, \"but the evidence for that is weak.\" For older students the picture is different: homework does seem to help, but only up to about two hours a night, after which the benefits disappear. Duarte adds that what matters most is the quality of the task rather than the time spent on it. She is also concerned about fairness. \"Homework tends to widen the gap between children whose parents can help them and children whose parents cannot,\" she says.\n\nNot everyone is persuaded. Mark Bellamy, who teaches maths at a secondary school that many Brookfield pupils go on to attend, has noticed a difference. \"They are keen and they read well,\" he says. \"But some of them find it hard when they arrive here and suddenly have homework in every subject. They have never had to organise their time.\" He believes primary schools should introduce small amounts of homework in the final year to prepare children for the change. \"It does not need to be much,\" he adds. \"Even one short task a week would help.\"\n\nAdeyemi accepts that this is a fair point, and the school is now considering a short weekly project for its oldest pupils. Test results, meanwhile, have stayed much the same as before the change, with reading scores slightly higher. For Adeyemi, that is enough. \"We were told that results would fall,\" she says. \"They haven't. And our children are happier. I don't know what more we could ask for.\""}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 28-30. Choose the correct letter, A, B, C or D. Write the correct letter in boxes 28-30 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"mcq","questions":[{"n":28,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What was the main reason the school stopped setting homework?","options":["A Teachers were spending too long on marking.","B It was causing arguments in families.","C Pupils were too tired after school.","D Test results had begun to fall."],"correct":1,"evidence":"homework came top by a long way","why":{"en":"Marking \"was never the main reason\". The \"final straw\" was the survey: homework caused the most arguments at home.","tr":"Ödev okumak \"hiçbir zaman asıl neden değildi\". \"Bardağı taşıran\" anket oldu: evdeki tartışmaların başında ödev geliyordu.","fa":"تصحیح تکلیف «هیچ‌وقت دلیل اصلی نبود». «تیر آخر» نظرسنجی بود: تکلیف بیشترین دعوا را در خانه ایجاد می‌کرد."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]},{"n":29,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"How was the change introduced?","options":["A only for the youngest pupils at first","B immediately, without discussion","C as a trial lasting one year","D after a vote by the pupils"],"correct":2,"evidence":"agreed to try the new approach for one year before making a final decision","why":{"en":"After two meetings for parents, the school \"agreed to try the new approach for one year\".","tr":"Veliler için yapılan iki toplantının ardından okul \"yeni yaklaşımı bir yıl denemeyi kabul etti\".","fa":"بعد از دو جلسه با والدین، مدرسه «پذیرفت روش تازه را یک سال امتحان کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":30,"kind":"mcq","prompt":"What does the writer say about the family projects?","options":["A They are not checked by teachers.","B They are compulsory for older pupils.","C Most families complete them every week.","D They have replaced daily reading."],"correct":0,"evidence":"None of these is checked or marked","why":{"en":"The projects are \"optional\" and \"none of these is checked or marked\".","tr":"Projeler \"isteğe bağlı\" ve \"hiçbiri kontrol edilmiyor ya da notlanmıyor\".","fa":"پروژه‌ها «اختیاری‌اند» و «هیچ‌کدام بررسی یا نمره‌دهی نمی‌شوند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 31-35. Look at the following statements (Questions 31-35) and the list of people below. Match each statement with the correct person, A-E. Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 31-35 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-features","bank":["A Ruth Adeyemi","B Gareth Lyle","C Sofia","D Ines Duarte","E Mark Bellamy"],"questions":[{"n":31,"kind":"match","prompt":"Homework can increase the differences between children from different homes.","correct":3,"evidence":"Homework tends to widen the gap","why":{"en":"Duarte: homework \"tends to widen the gap between children whose parents can help them and children whose parents cannot\".","tr":"Duarte: ödev \"ebeveyni yardım edebilen çocuklarla edemeyenler arasındaki farkı açma eğiliminde\".","fa":"دوارته: تکلیف «معمولاً شکاف بین بچه‌هایی که پدر و مادرشان می‌توانند کمک کنند و آن‌هایی که نمی‌توانند را بیشتر می‌کند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":32,"kind":"match","prompt":"Children now have time for more activities after school.","correct":1,"evidence":"Now they go to football training, help me cook, or just play outside","why":{"en":"Lyle: \"Now they go to football training, help me cook, or just play outside.\"","tr":"Lyle: \"Artık futbol antrenmanına gidiyorlar, yemek yapmama yardım ediyorlar ya da sadece dışarıda oynuyorlar.\"","fa":"لایل: «حالا می‌روند تمرین فوتبال، در آشپزی کمکم می‌کنند یا فقط بیرون بازی می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":33,"kind":"match","prompt":"Some pupils have difficulty when they move on to their next school.","correct":4,"evidence":"some of them find it hard when they arrive here","why":{"en":"Bellamy: \"some of them find it hard when they arrive here and suddenly have homework in every subject\".","tr":"Bellamy: \"bazıları buraya geldiklerinde ve birden her derste ödevleri olunca zorlanıyor\".","fa":"بلامی: «بعضی‌هایشان وقتی به این‌جا می‌رسند و ناگهان در همه‌ی درس‌ها تکلیف دارند به زحمت می‌افتند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":34,"kind":"match","prompt":"Reading for enjoyment teaches children more than worksheets do.","correct":0,"evidence":"A child who reads a book they love for twenty minutes learns more","why":{"en":"Adeyemi: a child reading a book they love \"learns more than a child who fills in a worksheet they hate\".","tr":"Adeyemi: sevdiği bir kitabı okuyan çocuk \"nefret ettiği bir çalışma kâğıdını dolduran çocuktan daha çok öğrenir\".","fa":"آدیمی: بچه‌ای که کتاب محبوبش را می‌خواند «بیشتر از بچه‌ای یاد می‌گیرد که برگه‌ای را پر می‌کند که از آن متنفر است»."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice"]},{"n":35,"kind":"match","prompt":"Evenings at home have become more peaceful.","correct":2,"evidence":"is that evenings are calmer","why":{"en":"Sofia: \"What she likes most... is that evenings are calmer.\" Lyle talks about time, not arguments.","tr":"Sofia: \"En çok hoşuna giden... akşamların daha sakin olması.\" Lyle tartışmalardan değil, zamandan söz ediyor.","fa":"سوفیا: «چیزی که بیشتر از همه دوست دارد... این است که عصرها آرام‌ترند». لایل از وقت حرف می‌زند، نه از دعوا."},"trap":["TR-whosevoice","TR-samewords"]}]},{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 36-40. Complete the summary below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the text for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 36-40 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"summary","summaryTitle":"What research says about homework","questions":[{"n":36,"kind":"gap","prompt":"For children under eleven, homework seems to have very little effect on ___.","accept":["achievement"],"limit":1,"evidence":"homework appears to have very little effect on achievement","why":{"en":"\"Homework appears to have very little effect on achievement.\"","tr":"\"Ödevin başarı üzerinde çok az etkisi var gibi görünüyor.\"","fa":"«به نظر می‌رسد تکلیف اثر خیلی کمی بر پیشرفت تحصیلی دارد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":37,"kind":"gap","prompt":"It may help them to develop study ___, but the evidence for this is weak.","accept":["habits"],"limit":1,"evidence":"helping children develop study habits","why":{"en":"\"Helping children develop study habits.\" Plural.","tr":"\"Çocukların çalışma alışkanlıkları geliştirmesine yardım etmek.\" Çoğul.","fa":"«کمک به بچه‌ها برای ساختن عادت‌های مطالعه». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":38,"kind":"gap","prompt":"For older students homework helps, but only up to about two ___ a night.","accept":["hours"],"limit":1,"evidence":"only up to about two hours a night","why":{"en":"\"Only up to about two hours a night, after which the benefits disappear.\"","tr":"\"Gecede yalnızca yaklaşık iki saate kadar, sonrasında faydalar kayboluyor.\"","fa":"«فقط تا حدود دو ساعت در شب؛ بعد از آن فایده‌ها از بین می‌روند»."},"trap":["TR-plural"]},{"n":39,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The ___ of a task matters more than the time spent on it.","accept":["quality"],"limit":1,"evidence":"what matters most is the quality of the task","why":{"en":"\"What matters most is the quality of the task rather than the time spent on it.\"","tr":"\"En önemli olan, harcanan zamandan çok görevin niteliği.\"","fa":"«مهم‌ترین چیز کیفیت تکلیف است، نه وقتی که صرفش می‌شود»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":40,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The researcher is also worried about ___.","accept":["fairness"],"limit":1,"evidence":"She is also concerned about fairness","why":{"en":"\"She is also concerned about fairness\": worried = concerned.","tr":"\"Adalet konusunda da endişeli\": worried = concerned.","fa":"«او درباره‌ی انصاف هم نگران است»: worried یعنی concerned."},"trap":["TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x06-r3-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"Homework tends to widen the gap between children.\" To widen the gap is to...","options":["close the difference","make the difference bigger","measure the difference"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"Widen = make wider; the gap = the difference.","tr":"Widen = genişletmek; the gap = fark.","fa":"widen یعنی گسترده‌تر کردن؛ the gap یعنی فاصله یا تفاوت."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"mornings are less rushed than before\". Which words in a text match?","options":["there is no longer a hurry before school","mornings now start earlier","mornings are busier than ever"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"No longer a hurry = less rushed.","tr":"\"No longer a hurry\" (artık acele yok) = \"less rushed\" (daha az telaşlı).","fa":"«no longer a hurry» (دیگر عجله‌ای نیست) یعنی «less rushed» (کم‌عجله‌تر)."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"Five people, A-E, and five statements, with \"NB You may use any letter more than once.\" What does this mean?","options":["each person is used exactly once","one statement may have two answers","one person may match two statements"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Letters can be reused, so a person can match more than one statement, and another may match none.","tr":"Harfler yeniden kullanılabilir; bir kişi birden fazla ifadeye uyabilir, başka biri hiçbirine uymayabilir.","fa":"حرف‌ها دوباره قابل استفاده‌اند؛ یک نفر ممکن است با بیش از یک جمله جور باشد و نفر دیگری با هیچ‌کدام."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"\"‘Some parents feared their children would fall behind,’ says the head teacher, ‘but our results show the opposite.’\" Who thinks the children fell behind?","options":["the head teacher","some parents","both"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The head teacher reports the parents’ fear and then disagrees.","tr":"Müdür velilerin korkusunu aktarıyor, sonra karşı çıkıyor.","fa":"مدیر ترس والدین را نقل می‌کند و بعد مخالفت می‌کند."}}],"id":"c-x06-r3-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-06","unit":"x06-r3"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
